<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:11:11 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>观看今年年度海洋摄影师大赛的九张令人惊叹的照片，展示海洋生物的威严</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-nine-stunning-images-from-this-years-ocean-photographer-of-the-year-contest-that-show-the-majesty-of-marine-life-180989489/</link><description>从海马的告别到拯救搁浅的鲸鱼，这些照片捕捉到了海洋生物的多样性和美丽，同时也捕捉到了它们面临的危险</description><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:15:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-nine-stunning-images-from-this-years-ocean-photographer-of-the-year-contest-that-show-the-majesty-of-marine-life-180989489/</guid></item><item><title>戴安娜王妃的“复仇礼服”近 30 年来首次拍卖</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/princess-dianas-revenge-dress-is-heading-to-auction-for-the-first-time-in-nearly-30-years-180989492/</link><description>这位时尚偶像在她当时分居的丈夫公开承认有外遇的同一天穿着这件无肩带丝绸连衣裙</description><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:58:56 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/princess-dianas-revenge-dress-is-heading-to-auction-for-the-first-time-in-nearly-30-years-180989492/</guid></item><item><title>一幅被纳粹掠夺的稀有画作，丢失了大约 80 年，现在出现在房地产清单中。现在，法官已下令将其归还给其合法继承人</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/A-Rare-Nazi-Looted-Painting-lost-for-Some-80-Years-Turned-Up-in-a-Real-Estate-Listing-Now-a-Judge-Has-Ordered-It-Returned-to-Its-Rightful-Heirs-180989488/</link><description>阿根廷一家法院在一项具有里程碑意义的裁决中裁定，贾科莫·切鲁蒂 (Giacomo Ceruti) 的《女士肖像》自 1945 年在阿姆斯特丹被盗以来一直失踪，将归还其真正的主人。</description><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:29:12 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/A-Rare-Nazi-Looted-Painting-lost-for-Some-80-Years-Turned-Up-in-a-Real-Estate-Listing-Now-a-Judge-Has-Ordered-It-Returned-to-Its-Rightful-Heirs-180989488/</guid></item><item><title>观看难以捉摸、飘逸飘逸的大鳍鱿鱼漂浮在加利福尼亚州中部附近的海底之上</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/watch-an-elusive-and-ethereal-bigfin-squid-float-above-the-seafloor-off-central-california-180989491/</link><description>这标志着人们首次在东北太平洋发现这种神秘生物。上个月，科学家在研究水下山脉附近海洋生物的探险中发现了它</description><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/watch-an-elusive-and-ethereal-bigfin-squid-float-above-the-seafloor-off-central-california-180989491/</guid></item><item><title>科学家在中国西南部发现了一批丹尼索瓦人化石和工具，让人们对我们已灭绝的表亲的生活有了前所未有的了解</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-find-a-trove-of-denisovan-fossils-and-tools-in-southwest-china-giving-an-unprecendented-glimpse-into-our-extinct-cousins-lives-180989483/</link><description>过去出土的神秘早期人类化石相对较少。两项新研究描述了 7 块丹尼索瓦人化石和 1,300 多件石器和骨器</description><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-find-a-trove-of-denisovan-fossils-and-tools-in-southwest-china-giving-an-unprecendented-glimpse-into-our-extinct-cousins-lives-180989483/</guid></item><item><title>一位芬兰金属探测器在他的家乡发现了一批维京时代的银器，感到震惊。然后他的探测器又响了</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-finnish-metal-detectorist-was-shocked-to-unearth-a-trove-of-viking-age-silver-in-his-hometown-then-his-detector-went-off-again-180989487/</link><description>这些文物总重 10 磅，估计已有 1,000 年历史，是芬兰当时最大的钱币宝藏</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:14:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-finnish-metal-detectorist-was-shocked-to-unearth-a-trove-of-viking-age-silver-in-his-hometown-then-his-detector-went-off-again-180989487/</guid></item><item><title>你经历过闷热的八月吗？你并不孤单。本月与有记录以来最热的全球气温持平</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/did-you-suffer-a-sweltering-august-you-werent-alone-it-tied-for-the-month-with-the-hottest-global-temperatures-on-record-180989482/</link><description>上个月平均气温为 62.53 华氏度，与 2023 年 7 月并列欧盟气候服务记录以来最炎热的月份</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:57:52 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/did-you-suffer-a-sweltering-august-you-werent-alone-it-tied-for-the-month-with-the-hottest-global-temperatures-on-record-180989482/</guid></item><item><title>设计师和计算机科学家创造了人类可以阅读但人工智能机器人无法阅读的新诱饵字体</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/designers-and-computer-scientists-create-new-decoy-fonts-that-humans-can-read-and-ai-bots-cannot-180989470/</link><description>为了防止人类书写的拖网和盗窃，字体制造商正在利用新旧幻觉来智胜大型语言模型</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:08:08 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/designers-and-computer-scientists-create-new-decoy-fonts-that-humans-can-read-and-ai-bots-cannot-180989470/</guid></item><item><title>古罗马最大的壁画和马赛克建筑群描绘了一座神秘的海上城市，2000 年后向公众开放</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ancient-romes-largest-fresco-and-mosaic-complex-featuring-depictions-of-a-mysterious-maritime-city-opens-to-the-public-after-2000-years-180989484/</link><description>这些大型艺术品创作于公元一世纪，于 20 世纪 90 年代在图拉真浴场的挖掘过程中被发现</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:31:29 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ancient-romes-largest-fresco-and-mosaic-complex-featuring-depictions-of-a-mysterious-maritime-city-opens-to-the-public-after-2000-years-180989484/</guid></item><item><title>考古学家在一位生活在 25,000 年前的狩猎采集者的牙齿中发现了世界上最古老的习惯性吸毒证据</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-discover-the-worlds-oldest-evidence-of-habitual-drug-use-in-the-teeth-of-a-hunter-gatherer-who-lived-up-to-25000-years-ago-180989485/</link><description>此人可能经常吸食槟榔，槟榔以其改变思维的特性而闻名，导致牙齿疾病恶化。研究人员表示，这一发现揭示了史前环境中的成瘾现象</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:12:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-discover-the-worlds-oldest-evidence-of-habitual-drug-use-in-the-teeth-of-a-hunter-gatherer-who-lived-up-to-25000-years-ago-180989485/</guid></item><item><title>几十年来，科学家们一直认为“美国猎豹”曾在北美漫游。事实证明，灭绝的猫科动物并不是猎豹</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-decades-scientists-thought-an-american-cheetah-once-roamed-north-america-ancient-turns-out-the-extinct-cat-wasnt-a-cheetah-180989465/</link><description>怀俄明州和加拿大育空地区发现的化石中的古代 DNA 表明，与现代猎豹相比，野猫更类似于现代美洲狮</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-decades-scientists-thought-an-american-cheetah-once-roamed-north-america-ancient-turns-out-the-extinct-cat-wasnt-a-cheetah-180989465/</guid></item><item><title>转基因猪肾使一名男子存活了创纪录的九个月，使他能够等待捐赠的人体器官</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-genetically-modified-pig-kidney-kept-a-man-alive-for-a-record-nine-months-allowing-him-to-wait-for-a-donated-human-organ-180989466/</link><description>动物器官使蒂姆·安德鲁斯 (Tim Andrews) 271 天无需接受透析，这也是猪肾首次被用作人体器官移植的桥梁</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-genetically-modified-pig-kidney-kept-a-man-alive-for-a-record-nine-months-allowing-him-to-wait-for-a-donated-human-organ-180989466/</guid></item><item><title>人工智能可能已经解决了一个长期存在的数学问题并获得了百万美元的奖金。它引发了关于谁获得荣誉的争议</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ai-may-have-solved-a-longstanding-math-problem-with-a-million-dollar-prize-it-ignited-a-controversy-over-who-gets-credit-180989472/</link><description>OpenAI 宣布了纳维-斯托克斯问题的解决方案。但它的人工智能模型是否可以使用两位致力于类似突破的数学家的数据？</description><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:23:25 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ai-may-have-solved-a-longstanding-math-problem-with-a-million-dollar-prize-it-ignited-a-controversy-over-who-gets-credit-180989472/</guid></item><item><title>美国女童子军宣布推出首个标志性饼干系列——专为狗设计的饼干</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/girl-scouts-of-america-announces-a-first-for-its-iconic-cookie-lineup-one-created-exclusively-for-dogs-180989479/</link><description>该组织在 109 年的饼干销售历史上首次为四足朋友提供定制甜点</description><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:28:28 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/girl-scouts-of-america-announces-a-first-for-its-iconic-cookie-lineup-one-created-exclusively-for-dogs-180989479/</guid></item><item><title>澳大利亚第二小的岩袋鼠在50年未见的地区再次出现</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/australias-second-smallest-rock-wallaby-reappears-in-a-region-where-it-had-not-been-seen-for-50-years-180989469/</link><description>濒临灭绝的纳巴勒克蜥蜴不容易被发现，也很难与类似物种区分开来。但一个研究小组对这些动物进行了新的检测，这为“它们的长期生存提供了好消息”</description><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:00:37 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/australias-second-smallest-rock-wallaby-reappears-in-a-region-where-it-had-not-been-seen-for-50-years-180989469/</guid></item><item><title>大英图书馆将世界最畅销小说家阿加莎·克里斯蒂的一生带入显微镜下</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-life-of-agatha-christie-the-worlds-best-selling-novelist-goes-under-the-microscope-at-the-british-library-180989480/</link><description>即将在伦敦举行的展览将通过信件、照片、打字机和夏威夷冲浪板的复制品来探索克里斯蒂“非凡”经历的广度</description><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:55:05 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-life-of-agatha-christie-the-worlds-best-selling-novelist-goes-under-the-microscope-at-the-british-library-180989480/</guid></item><item><title>塔斯马尼亚虎被称为牲畜杀手。新的研究挑战神话</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-tasmanian-tiger-was-branded-a-livestock-killer-new-research-challenges-that-myth-180989473/</link><description>袋狼具有强大的咬合力，适合捕捉袋狸等中小型猎物，而不是像欧洲殖民者担心的那样捕食羊和牛等大型动物</description><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:43:58 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-tasmanian-tiger-was-branded-a-livestock-killer-new-research-challenges-that-myth-180989473/</guid></item><item><title>这条蛇的尾巴尖看起来像蜘蛛。但它的内部骨骼却“异常正常”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-tip-of-this-snakes-tail-looks-like-a-spider-but-inside-its-bones-are-bizarrely-normal-180989478/</link><description>高科技扫描首次详细展示了蜘蛛尾角毒蛇的内部解剖结构。这些发现揭示了鲜为人知的蛇椎骨，并强调了从骨骼预测动物的样子的难度</description><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 16:06:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-tip-of-this-snakes-tail-looks-like-a-spider-but-inside-its-bones-are-bizarrely-normal-180989478/</guid></item><item><title>“神奇”蘑菇中发现的迷幻化合物可能会预防化疗引起的神经损伤和疼痛</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-psychedelic-compound-found-in-magic-mushrooms-might-prevent-debilitating-nerve-damage-and-pain-caused-by-chemotherapy-180989457/</link><description>一项针对小鼠和人体组织的研究表明，裸盖菇素可以预防周围神经病变，这是化疗的常见副作用。研究结果非常有希望，研究人员今年开始进行中期临床试验</description><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:48:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-psychedelic-compound-found-in-magic-mushrooms-might-prevent-debilitating-nerve-damage-and-pain-caused-by-chemotherapy-180989457/</guid></item><item><title>考古学家发现了一个新石器时代的人类骑着豹子的雕塑，这“与我们以前遇到过的任何东西都不一样”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-uncover-a-neolithic-sculpture-of-a-human-riding-a-leopard-thats-unlike-anything-we-have-encountered-before-180989477/</link><description>这件文物是在土耳其东南部一处拥有 11,000 年历史的卡拉汉泰佩 (Karahan Tepe) 遗址的挖掘过程中发现的。这座 2.3 英尺高的雕塑早在文字发明之前就已创作，其用途仍是一个谜</description><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:09:55 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-uncover-a-neolithic-sculpture-of-a-human-riding-a-leopard-thats-unlike-anything-we-have-encountered-before-180989477/</guid></item></channel></rss>